  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Development Organisation - OD Grant</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Formerly African Family Support Services (AFSS), Community Development Organisation (CDO) is a Diaspora-led organisation supporting disadvantaged communities in the UK and Uganda. In Uganda CDO focuses on providing support and services for orphans and vulnerable children, and people affected by HIV/AIDS. In 2010 CDO undertook an organisational review funded by the Modernisation Fund, which identified their governance structure, long-term strategy, and relationships with their partners as priority areas for development. As recommended they have changed their status to a charitable company limited by guarantee adopting a new legal structure and changing their name. Through this application they aim to address the other gaps identified by the review, focusing on strengthening governance, developing a strategic plan, developing fundraising and communications strategies, and reviewing financial management and monitoring and evaluation systems.</narrative>
  </description>
